        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 23:27:54.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20984 lnet: check Netlink attributes fit in the message",
        "message": "LU-20984 lnet: check Netlink attributes fit in the message\n\nThe LNet Netlink handlers walk the nested attributes of a request\nusing the length stored in its first attribute header, which was\nnever compared with the length of the message received.  They also\nstep to a value attribute with nla_next() and read it without\nchecking that it is still within the enclosing attribute.\nA malformed request could therefore make the parser read past the\nend of the message.\n\nCheck the first attribute with nla_ok() against the message length\nbefore walking it, and check every attribute reached by nla_next()\nbefore using it.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 8f8f6e2f36e5 (\"LU-10003 lnet: use Netlink to support old and new NI APIs.\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I24e92280785004a4472e0d3d9a66e986157a6431\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
